# Regression probes on the complete living KB. New names test the mechanics
# without relying on the malformed propositions saved by the original session.
[test rejected assertions do not enter the parallel semantic store]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset
!timeout 30
# 26 settembre 2026: un identificatore unito («print_q») ora e' un nome e la
# lezione entra (P9/P7); il rifiuto si prova con una frase che resta rifiutata
# (oggetto frasale, P3).
> The probeq setting controls whether probe errors appear in the probe output.
<~ didn't keep
!query! semantic_binding(binary(control), probeq_setting_controls_whether_probe_errors, object(probe_output))
> What does probeq control?
<! probe output

[test negation is not a positive subject]
!reset
!timeout 30
> A probewarning does not stop the probedaemon.
!query! semantic_binding(binary(stop), probewarning_does_not, object(probedaemon))
> What stops the probedaemon?
<! Probewarning
> A probeguard stops the probedaemon.
> What stops the probedaemon?
<~ probeguard
<! does not

[test contact noun preserves the whole entity and relation direction]
!reset
!timeout 30
> A missing semicolon causes a parse error, so a parse error is its symptom.
> What is the symptom of a missing semicolon?
<~ parse error
> What is the symptom of output before the header function?
<! named block of code
> What is the symptom of a parse error?
<! missing semicolon

[test a taught relation accepts a polar value and remains open world]
!reset
!timeout 30
> probe port is a relation
> The probe port of probeadapter is 9123.
> What is the probe port of probeadapter?
<~ 9123
> Is 9123 the probe port of probeadapter?
<~ Yes
> Is 9124 the probe port of probeadapter?
<~ don't know
> forget that the probe port of probeadapter is 9123
> Is 9123 the probe port of probeadapter?
<! Yes

[test inverse named relation keeps its declared direction]
!reset
!timeout 30
> The capital of probeprovince is probecity.
> Is probecity the capital of probeprovince?
<~ Yes
> Is probeprovince the capital of probecity?
<! Yes

[test proof questions still work]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Why is Socrates a man?
<~ man

# 26 settembre 2026 — le riparazioni della seconda passata, con la conoscenza
# vera della sessione PHP (docs/sessions/live/2026-09-26-php-debug.log).
[test an identifier written as one token is a name]
!reset
!timeout 30
> The default value of memory_limit is 128 megabytes.
<~ Learned
> What is the default value of memory_limit?
<~ 128 megabytes

[test an adjective of relation closes only before its preposition]
!reset
!timeout 30
> A fatal error stops the script.
<~ Learned
> Does a fatal error stop the script?
<~ Yes
> Nicotine is fatal to insects.
> What is nicotine fatal to?
<~ Insects

[test a declared compound name keeps its verb-like head]
!reset
!timeout 30
> A stack trace is a list.
<~ Learned
> A stack trace shows the sequence of function calls.
<~ Learned
> What shows the sequence of function calls?
<~ stack trace
> Explain this stack trace.
<~ paste it here

[test a where question never receives a verdict]
!reset
!timeout 30
> OPcache stores compiled bytecode in shared memory.
> Where does OPcache store compiled bytecode?
<! Yes
<! Compiled bytecode
> Does OPcache store compiled bytecode?
<~ Yes
# e l'interrogativo davanti chiede ancora un VALORE (regressione della prima
# correzione di P13, trovata da docs/labs/l3/I5/strumenti.p0t)
> Einstein was born in Ulm.
> Where was Einstein born?
<~ ulm

[test is its N names a relation not a class]
!reset
!timeout 30
> A missing semicolon causes a parse error, so a parse error is its symptom.
<! is a symptom
> What is the capital of France?
<~ Paris
